@startuml
title Multi-Hybrid Cloud DFS: Data Partitions and Replication

actor User

package "Multi-Hybrid Cloud Environment" {

  cloud "Public Cloud A" {
    rectangle "DFS Partition A1\n(Storage & Compute)" as PartitionA1
    rectangle "DFS Partition A2\n(Storage & Compute)" as PartitionA2
  }

  cloud "Public Cloud B" {
    rectangle "DFS Partition B1\n(Storage & Compute)" as PartitionB1
  }

  package "On-Prem Data Center" {
    rectangle "DFS Partition C1\n(Storage & Compute)" as PartitionC1
    rectangle "DFS Partition C2\n(Storage & Compute)" as PartitionC2
  }
}

User --> PartitionA1 : Access files
User --> PartitionC1

PartitionA1 <--> PartitionB1 : Data Replication
PartitionA2 <--> PartitionC2 : Data Replication
PartitionB1 <--> PartitionC1 : Data Replication

note right of PartitionA1
  Replication for fault tolerance\nand data locality
end note

note right of PartitionC1
  On-premises storage with sync\nacross clouds
end note

@enduml